    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0570" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg550"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 11, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With reference to the despatch of the
                    6th ultimo, addressed to your lordship by E. M. Archibald, esq., her Majesty’s
                    consul at New York, in regard to the treatment of prisoners at Fort Lafayette, a
                    copy of which was left at this department,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d305-f1"/> I
                    have the honor to enclose, in reply, a copy of a communication from the War
                    Department, to which department the matter was referred for investigation.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, my lord, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d305-a1.xml" xpointer="d305-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d305-f1" n="*" xml:id="d305-f1-content">
                <p>The despatch above referred to will be found in the order of its date in this
                    correspondence.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
